<title>JAPAN: NCB shares up on plans to raise capital.</title>
<headline>NCB shares up on plans to raise capital.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Nippon Credit Bank Ltd (NCB) rose slightly on Wednesday morning, after the bank announced late on Tuesday details of a plan to increase its capital by 290.7 billion yen through new share issues.</p>
<p>NCB's share price, which had been hit hard recently despite the bank's announcement of a restructuring plan, climbed six yen to 176 by 0110 GMT.</p>
<p>Its turnover of 3.391 million was the heaviest on the first section of the Tokyo Stock Exchange.</p>
